item.text:
{
  "record_digest": "bb68ae43bd55975505d92d7537d72db488d1443f853c2406528c043c1caeadd3",
  "proposed": 18,
  "replacements": [
    {
      "field": "/work_item/gloss",
      "section_digest": "465d097cd588ae9c47341609b996d1d9537d217ee5fccbeb09e2210b423eede2",
      "text": "a test that keeps the routing table the only model inventory"
    },
    {
      "field": "/summary",
      "section_digest": "c688dc7904ae053a51f3da21dcb4a53df594f927b231b2c33ad31cd11e74cab4",
      "text": "The routing table in the delegation skill is meant to be the only inventory of model ids. Nothing enforced that. A new test suite now reads the Markdown files under `src/`, except those under an `evals` or `node_modules` directory. The suite fails `make ci` on a model id the table does not list. Anthropic aliases such as `sonnet` are not caught."
    },
    {
      "field": "/risk/rows/0/failure",
      "section_digest": "14dae3b25507ce6f19322c825a1daf4061a7b8b0cfbdddacdbe6db1dcdbfb01d",
      "text": "Rejecting a word that is not a model id makes the test block every pull request."
    },
    {
      "field": "/risk/rows/0/evidence",
      "section_digest": "e4e652706a0bc54e694c87f612e4805a9018744afef1b98e8fc30b1c144cb299",
      "text": "The patterns are case-sensitive. 94 files in the real repository tree pass the test."
    },
    {
      "field": "/risk/rows/0/recovery",
      "section_digest": "57b5ef5e6827a9b71e8f96369b02f3e8408d26d2ce2984b702fdd98272670c27",
      "text": "Nothing ships from the test file. Therefore, delete it."
    },
    {
      "field": "/risk/rows/1/evidence",
      "section_digest": "f8f61279cd5d60333f44df5d322dab50ab5a8a15d6cabd5d4922a3667a78ebec",
      "text": "An unlisted id appended to a skill made `make content-tests` exit 2. The command named the line."
    },
    {
      "field": "/changes/0/topic",
      "section_digest": "1c53bc1b8832ee518cfbec7090d2e8f24509f48d2ea20b39dd6f8048f03dcf80",
      "text": "The test suite"
    },
    {
      "field": "/changes/0/text",
      "section_digest": "27153b2419b2c8bfd1f0235ff52922c4d64ba2610fec9f111481f1ef964d30a2",
      "text": "A pytest test suite beside the delegation skill fails on an unlisted model id. It fails on a table row elsewhere that names any id. It fails on a routing table that changes shape."
    },
    {
      "field": "/changes/1/text",
      "section_digest": "2e0def8823310cda9fc7988c8fccc0496ef15cc5edc3ee2511ab7a01e67658fe",
      "text": "Each vendor naming scheme has one case-sensitive pattern. Consequently, a family name in prose is not an id."
    },
    {
      "field": "/changes/2/text",
      "section_digest": "7106267a4b7c81e14fc67720ad37266acbe9b056d06647abe57c748106e782f6",
      "text": "The test allows two tables in the routing file. Therefore, the routing file's Providers table became a list."
    },
    {
      "field": "/discovered/rows/0/reason",
      "section_digest": "868e4313ef1bbdd9195ded714c62962f17282afe029401f0e4c13348830a975d",
      "text": "The spec defines ids by vendor naming scheme. An alias does not follow a vendor naming scheme."
    },
    {
      "field": "/criteria/0/promise",
      "section_digest": "17717dea7bd2fdeae85e3a07eabe47bbcbf241853012a05bc50a4e8ad94047e8",
      "text": "An unlisted model id in any Markdown file the test reads under `src/` causes a failure. The failure names the file and the id."
    },
    {
      "field": "/criteria/1/promise",
      "section_digest": "fd9bbfd28cf41d76b83ad106291dd40081f0dd51c7ee3bd7c1dd9d451e827df8",
      "text": "The landed repository tree passes."
    },
    {
      "field": "/criteria/2/promise",
      "section_digest": "16977f38fd6f48e9a8aeb59ee6d7dc0c777f803ccf55387ab81fc56f528bd279",
      "text": "A fenced example (an example in a Markdown code block) with a listed id fails once its routing-table row is removed."
    },
    {
      "field": "/criteria/4/promise",
      "section_digest": "4285235cade12787cf824747a95e9a2cf67d64a4b932a7531452c1a094808ef0",
      "text": "An absent or empty routing table causes a failure. The failure names the routing table."
    },
    {
      "field": "/criteria/5/promise",
      "section_digest": "75cc808240ee9324f5b1196c94e21c6c9b6b2021f51d4f960cd3d198fc72d5f0",
      "text": "A table row outside the routing table that names a listed id fails. The same id in prose passes."
    },
    {
      "field": "/commit/change",
      "section_digest": "1fc1557208855e5f2bda009d4ab0e68f9de71602b90f5f83375fc14970b8e452",
      "text": "A pytest test suite beside the delegation skill reads every Markdown file under src/, except those under an evals or node_modules directory. It fails on an unlisted model id, a table row elsewhere naming a model id, or a routing table with changed shape. The suite allows two tables in the routing file. Therefore, the file's Providers table becomes a list."
    },
    {
      "field": "/commit/verification",
      "section_digest": "e18309e147af46095ddceabe921bbbe68910073084ebb396ea5c7968b73cc2a9",
      "text": "make ci exits 0 at the head (the current commit). 20 content suites pass. All 34 cases fail against a stub lint (a checker returning no files or violations). All pass at the head. One unlisted id appended to a skill made the gate exit 2. The gate named the line. Anthropic aliases are not caught. No review round ran."
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "field": "/summary",
      "question": "Please add a separate Heads-up row for the uncaught Anthropic aliases and a row for the excluded `evals` and `node_modules` directories. Check 7 requires caveats to have their own rows; the existing Heads-up row covers only the missing review round. Keep these qualifications in the summary as well."
    },
    {
      "field": "/design_notes",
      "question": "What do PEP 723 and the tier grid mean here? The record does not supply their meanings. Please provide parenthetical explanations so this section can be edited faithfully."
    }
  ]
}
